WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.035
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.335 --> 00:00:09.756
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.056 --> 00:00:16.169
Unit two: Present Perfect and Duration. Today you will talk about experiences and unfinished time.

4
00:00:16.469 --> 00:00:18.958
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.237
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:25.259
Experience.

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.830
Experience means something you have done.

8
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.300
I have a lot of experience.

9
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:34.778
Your turn. Say: Experience.

10
00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:39.052
Experience.

11
00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:40.760
Already.

12
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.436
Already means before now.

13
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.539
I have already eaten.

14
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.431
Your turn. Say: Already.

15
00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.245
Already.

16
00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:53.694
Yet.

17
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:56.207
Yet means until now.

18
00:00:56.817 --> 00:00:58.352
I have not finished yet.

19
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.242
Your turn. Say: Yet.

20
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:04.822
Yet.

21
00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:06.550
Since.

22
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.968
Since means from a point in the past.

23
00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:13.279
I have lived here since 2018.

24
00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:16.280
Your turn. Say: Since.

25
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.053
Since.

26
00:01:20.817 --> 00:01:21.597
For.

27
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:24.513
For means during a period of time.

28
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.012
I have studied for two years.

29
00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:30.315
Your turn. Say: For.

30
00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:33.936
For.

31
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:35.719
Recently.

32
00:01:36.717 --> 00:01:38.647
Recently means not long ago.

33
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.727
I have recently moved.

34
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:43.853
Your turn. Say: Recently.

35
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.643
Recently.

36
00:01:48.383 --> 00:01:49.175
Ever.

37
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.695
Ever means at any time.

38
00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:53.610
Have you ever flown?

39
00:01:54.217 --> 00:01:56.230
Your turn. Say: Ever.

40
00:01:59.067 --> 00:01:59.812
Ever.

41
00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.330
Never.

42
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:04.026
Never means at no time.

43
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:06.245
I have never seen snow.

44
00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.340
Your turn. Say: Never.

45
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:12.969
Never.

46
00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:17.673
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.517 --> 00:02:21.015
Visal, when do I use the present perfect?

48
00:02:22.117 --> 00:02:35.540
Use it for experiences up to now, such as I have visited Siem Reap, and for situations that began in the past and continue now, such as I have lived here for ten years.

49
00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.253
What is the difference between since and for?

50
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:52.209
Use since with a starting point, such as since 2020 or since Monday. Use for with a length of time, such as for three years or for two hours.

51
00:02:53.317 --> 00:02:55.363
Can I say I have seen him yesterday?

52
00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:10.285
No. When you give a finished time, use the past simple: I saw him yesterday. The present perfect cannot be used with yesterday, last week or in 2019.

53
00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:13.061
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:17.251
Grammar focus: have and has plus past participle.

55
00:03:17.551 --> 00:03:18.785
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.483 --> 00:03:22.145
I have lived here since 2018.

57
00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.235
She has studied English for three years.

58
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:33.487
Use have or has with the past participle. Use since for a starting point and for for a length of time. Do not use a finished time.

59
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.982
Be careful! Don't say: I have seen him yesterday.

60
00:03:39.933 --> 00:03:42.014
Say: I saw him yesterday.

61
00:03:42.314 --> 00:03:44.511
Finished time: past simple.

62
00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.964
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.162
Years in Phnom Penh.

64
00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:53.844
Chenda has lived in Phnom Penh since 2018.

65
00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:57.123
She has studied English for four years.

66
00:03:58.133 --> 00:03:59.901
She has never travelled abroad.

67
00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.737
She has already finished her homework.

68
00:04:03.733 --> 00:04:05.698
She has not heard the results yet.

69
00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.941
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:11.783 --> 00:04:13.446
Since is used with a blank.

71
00:04:13.746 --> 00:04:17.643
A, length. B, number only. C, starting point.

72
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.618
The answer is C: starting point.

73
00:04:24.783 --> 00:04:27.154
I have studied here blank two years.

74
00:04:27.454 --> 00:04:30.353
A, for. B, since. C, at.

75
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.516
The answer is A: for.

76
00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:37.848
Which is correct?

77
00:04:38.148 --> 00:04:43.474
A, I see him yesterday.. B, I saw him yesterday.. C, I have seen him yesterday..

78
00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.520
The answer is B: I saw him yesterday..

79
00:04:50.683 --> 00:04:52.184
Never means blank.

80
00:04:52.484 --> 00:04:56.021
A, always. B, often. C, at no time.

81
00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.706
The answer is C: at no time.

82
00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.999
Chenda has lived in the city blank 2018.

83
00:05:06.299 --> 00:05:09.442
A, since. B, for. C, in.

84
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.104
The answer is A: since.

85
00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:19.742
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:22.722
How long have you studied English?

87
00:05:31.517 --> 00:05:33.110
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:43.228
I have studied English for six years. I started in primary school and I have practised every week since then. I have never missed an English class.

89
00:05:43.528 --> 00:05:45.179
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:51.116
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and have and has plus past participle.

91
00:05:51.416 --> 00:05:55.322
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

92
00:05:55.622 --> 00:05:58.112
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

93
00:05:58.412 --> 00:06:01.099
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

